<%# Article-history pilot: one covered article, in reading order (the owner, via Sol 2026-11-20 16:42:25Z). Its picker
    when the reader opened it, the notes the archive date needs (none on the live page) and the chosen wording's
    period stand outside the legal text; then the legal text, at the full width of the article (the owner's design of
    2026-11-21, via Sol 07:00:09Z: no icon and no column of its own; the number opens the article's menu, and its
    History item follows the hidden step link). The legal text, #article-text-<permalink> (what the copy actions read),
    is print_article's output untouched: the live row on the current-law page (live: [text, title, type]), else the
    wording the archive gives or the reader chose. With a comparison, the words changed against the wording before
    are shown in its place, after the article's identifier so its menu stays at hand, and the chosen wording stays
    the copied text; at the oldest wording there is none, so the text stays visible with a short note. Right after Close,
    data-history-return-focus asks for the focus back on the number (history_links_controller.js).
    Locals: history (HistoryPilotHelper::ArticleState), permalink, numac, live (optional). %>
<% key = history.key %>
<% live = local_assigns[:live] %>
<% if history_open?(key) %><%= render 'laws/history_picker', history: history, permalink: permalink %><% end %>
<% unless history.live? %><%= render 'laws/history_notes', history: history %><% end %>
<% if history.chosen %>
  <p class="not-prose mb-1 text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300" data-history-chosen="<%= key %>"><%= (history_label(:version_label) % { period: history_period(history.selected) }).upcase_first %><% if history.off_date %> (<%= history_label(:off_date) % { date: history_day(@history_as_of) } %>)<% end %></p>
<% end %>
<% printed = if history.live? && live
               print_article(*live, source_numac: numac)
             elsif history.shown_body
               print_article(history.shown_body, key, 'ART', source_numac: numac)
             end %>
<% comparing = @history_compare.include?(key) && history.shown_body %>
<% if comparing && !history.compare_base %>
  <p class="not-prose mb-1 text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300" data-history-no-previous><%= history_label(:no_previous) %></p>
<% end %>
<div data-history-row="<%= key %>" data-history-state="<%= history_rendered_state(key) %>" <%= tag.attributes(data: { history_return_focus: ('' if history_focus?(key, 'close')) }) %>>
  <%= render 'laws/history_link', history: history, permalink: permalink %>
  <% if comparing && history.compare_base %>
    <%= render 'laws/history_diff', key: key, old_body: history.compare_base.body, new_body: history.shown_body %>
    <div id="article-text-<%= permalink %>" hidden data-history-copy-text><%= printed %></div>
  <% elsif printed %>
    <div id="article-text-<%= permalink %>"><%= printed %></div>
  <% else %>
    <%# No wording on the archive date (a gap): the identifier alone keeps History at hand; the menu then offers no copy
        of a wording that is not there (Sol 2026-11-21 10:09:36Z). %>
    <%= render 'laws/history_identifier', identifier: history_identifier(key) %>
  <% end %>
</div>
